      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T13:54:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- Issue: The GC thread sleeps while holding the device lock, and the device has one shared delay slot. rtd_pause takes everything queued, including flash time that I/O commands added. So the GC thread can end up sleeping off I/O time while holding the lock. Meanwhile, the next FTL call from a coroutine waits on LOCK_DEVICE, a pthread mutex, which freezes QEMU\u0027s whole main loop, including vCPU MMIO and other devices. Also, the I/O command whose time GC took finishes with no delay, so per-command latency becomes unpredictable.\n  - Fix: Give GC its own slot (rtd_init(2, …), with slot 1 for GC) so its pause only waits out GC flash time. Or have GC pause after UNLOCK_DEVICE.",
      "revId": "f1d14ba82b3f7227d1965d9c48bc608fc326fbf7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
